rem Modular Cubes, part 1
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=271
rem Sum the x with 1 < x < n and x^3 = 1
rem mod n, where n is the product of the
rem primes up to Top

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

option Top integer = 43

rem The roots of x^3 = 1 mod n pair up
rem across the primes by the Chinese
rem remainder theorem: root r mod p
rem becomes r (n / p) (n / p)^-1 mod n,
rem and the roots are the sums mod n of
rem one such term per prime.
Ps = primes to Top array
N = Ps reduce *
Sums = array 0
for P in Ps
  Xs = 0 till P array
  Cube = (Xs * Xs * Xs) mod P
  Roots = Xs filter (Cube equal 1) array
  Q = N // P
  Inv = (Q mod P) (P - 2) P powmod
  Terms = (Roots * Q * Inv) mod N
  Rows = Sums len
  Col = Sums reshape Rows 1
  Both = (Col + Terms) mod N
  Cells = Rows * (Terms len)
  Sums = Both reshape Cells
end
Answer = Sums sum - 1
Answer print
